{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Shdn2vuQ3QrseHWbrBiUb6","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have successfully read all 11 files. Here is the complete contents of each file:\n\n## 1. PQCgenKAT_sign.c\nThis file contains the KAT (Known Answer Test) generation code for signature schemes. It includes conditional compilation for different hash functions (BLAKE, HARAKA, SHA2, SHAKE) and implements transcript-based KAT generation with iterative signature testing.\n\n## 2. sign.c\nMain signature implementation file containing:\n- `crypto_sign_secretkeybytes()` - returns secret key size\n- `crypto_sign_publickeybytes()` - returns public key size\n- `crypto_sign_bytes()` - returns signature size\n- `crypto_sign_seedbytes()` - returns seed size\n- `crypto_sign_seed_keypair()` - generates keypair from seed\n- `crypto_sign_keypair()` - generates random keypair\n- `crypto_sign_signature()` - creates detached signature\n- `crypto_sign_verify()` - verifies detached signature\n- `crypto_sign()` - creates signature with message\n- `crypto_sign_open()` - verifies and extracts message\n\n## 3. address.c\nAddress manipulation functions for SPHINCS+:\n- `set_layer_addr()` - sets Merkle tree layer\n- `set_tree_addr()` - sets tree address\n- `set_type()` - sets hash type\n- `copy_subtree_addr()` - copies layer/tree fields\n- `set_keypair_addr()` - sets OTS keypair index\n- `copy_keypair_addr()` - copies keypair fields\n- `set_chain_addr()` - sets chain address\n- `set_hash_addr()` - sets hash position\n- `set_tree_height()` - sets node height\n- `set_tree_index()` - sets node distance from left edge\n\n## 4. fors.c\nFORS (Forest of Random Subsets) implementation:\n- `fors_gen_leafx1()` - generates single FORS leaf\n- `message_to_indices()` - converts message to tree indices\n- `fors_sign()` - signs message using FORS\n- `fors_pk_from_sig()` - derives FORS public key from signature\n\n## 5. merkle.c\nMerkle tree operations:\n- `ull_to_bytes()` - converts unsigned long long to big-endian bytes\n- `u32_to_bytes()` - converts uint32_t to bytes\n- `bytes_to_ull()` - converts bytes to unsigned long long\n- `compute_root()` - computes root node from leaf and auth path\n- `treehash()` - generates authentication path and root using TreeHash algorithm\n\n## 6. utils.c (actually part of merkle.c contents shown)\nContains utility functions for byte conversion and Merkle tree computations.\n\n## 7. utilsx1.c\nOptimized x1 (single-instance) utility functions for WOTS and FORS tree hashing:\n- `wots_treehashx1()` - WOTS tree hash implementation\n- `fors_treehashx1()` - FORS tree hash implementation with stack-based node generation\n\n## 8. wots.c\nWOTS+ (Winternitz One-Time Signature) implementation:\n- `gen_chain()` - computes chaining function\n- `base_w()` - interprets bytes as base-w integers\n- `wots_checksum()` - computes WOTS+ checksum\n- `chain_lengths()` - derives chain lengths from message\n- `wots_pk_from_sig()` - computes WOTS public key from signature\n\n## 9. wotsx1.c\nOptimized x1 WOTS leaf generation:\n- `wots_gen_leafx1()` - generates WOTS public key and signature (if signing) for a single leaf\n\n## 10. randombytes.c\nRandom byte generation using `/dev/urandom`:\n- `randombytes()` - reads random bytes from `/dev/urandom` with retry logic for failures\n\n## 11. rng.c\nDRBG (Deterministic Random Bit Generator) implementation using AES-256-CTR:\n- `seedexpander_init()` - initializes AES XOF context\n- `seedexpander()` - expands seed using AES XOF\n- `AES256_ECB()` - AES-256 ECB encryption using OpenSSL\n- `randombytes_init()` - initializes DRBG with entropy and optional personalization\n- `randombytes()` - generates random bytes using AES-256-CTR-DRBG\n- `AES256_CTR_DRBG_Update()` - updates DRBG state\n\nAll files have been read completely as requested."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37e9594e-3af4-481c-abaf-bfc8535b5484","uuid":"4ffbb551-7d14-49be-85db-5645f459c73