ezeblocks(output: &mut [u8], nblocks: usize, s: &mut [u64; 25])`\n\nThe KeccakF1600_StatePermute function has 24 round constants:\n```\n0x0000000000000001, 0x0000000000008082,\n0x800000000000808a, 0x8000000080008000,\n0x000000000000808b, 0x0000000080000001,\n0x8000000080008081, 0x8000000000008009,\n0x000000000000008a, 0x0000000000000088,\n0x0000000080008009, 0x000000008000000a,\n0x000000008000808b, 0x800000000000008b,\n0x8000000000008089, 0x8000000000008003,\n0x8000000000008002, 0x8000000000000080,\n0x000000000000800a, 0x800000008000000a,\n0x8000000080008081, 0x8000000000008080,\n0x0000000080000001, 0x8000000080008008,\n```\n\nThe ROL macro: `(a << offset) ^ (a >> (64 - offset))`\n\nThe permutation processes two rounds at a time with 25 state variables named Aba,Abe,Abi,Abo,Abu, Aga..Asu and intermediate E variants. It's a direct translation of the C code.\n\nThe keccak_inc_absorb incremental absorb implementation:\n- s_inc[25] stores the count of non-absorbed bytes\n- While mlen + s_inc[25] >= r: XOR bytes into state at correct positions, permute, advance\n- Remaining bytes: XOR into state, increment s_inc[25]\n- Key detail: bytes are XORed into the state in little-endian u64 layout: `s_inc[(pos) >> 3] ^= (u64)m[i] << (8 * (pos & 0x07))`\n\nThe keccak_inc_squeeze implementation:\n- First consume remaining bytes from previous squeeze\n- Then squeeze blocks: permute, extract bytes\n- s_inc[25] tracks remaining bytes in current block\n\nMake sure the implementation is EXACTLY matching the C code behavior for byte-identical output. Use wrapping arithmetic for u64 operations.\n\nWrite ONLY the file content, no explanations."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2723,"cache_read_input_tokens":149704,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2723},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context