{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ef3LSp4AmxuqFce9TB19nc","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The file has been written at `/tmp/harvest-translate-qHL6TU/translated_rust/src/sha2_impl.rs`. It implements:\n\n- Big-endian load/store helpers (`load_bigendian_32/64`, `store_bigendian_32/64`)\n- SHA-256 and SHA-512 round constants (K256, K512)\n- SHA-256/512 compression helper functions (Ch, Maj, Sigma0/1, sigma0/1 for both 32-bit and 64-bit variants)\n- `crypto_hashblocks_sha256` and `crypto_hashblocks_sha512` block compression functions\n- Incremental hashing API: `sha256_inc_init/blocks/finalize` and `sha512_inc_init/blocks/finalize`\n- One-shot `sha256` and `sha512`\n- `mgf1_256` and `mgf1_512` using `crate::utils::u32_to_bytes` for the counter\n- `seed_state` with conditional SHA-512 seeding via `#[cfg]`\n\nAll arithmetic uses wrapping operations (`.wrapping_add()`, `.rotate_right()`). The padding follows the C conventions with `bytes >> 53` style encoding for SHA-256 and `bytes >> 61` style for SHA-512."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ae5afc86d5b31e6aa (use SendMessage with to: 'ae5afc86d5b31e6aa' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 38752\ntool_uses: 11\nduration_ms: 209634</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37e9594e-3af4-481c-abaf-bfc8535b5484","uuid":"2968ebd9-4aec-4bef-9a59-08dfbc885206","timestamp":"2026-04-02T08:53:14.617Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Write the file /tmp/harvest-translate-qHL6TU/translated_rust/src/sha2_impl.rs\n\nThis is a byte-identical Rust translation of sha2.c. It implements SHA-256 and SHA-512 with incremental hashing API plus MGF1 functions.\n\nThe module structure:\n\n```rust\n#![allow(non_snake_case)]\n```\n\nFunctions to implement (all pub):\n1. `sha256_inc_init(state: &mut [u8; 40])` - init with IV, zero counter at bytes 32-39\n2. `sha256_inc_blocks(state: &mut [u8; 40], inp: &[u8], inblocks: usize)` - process full 64-byte blocks\n3. `sha256_inc_finalize(out: &mut [u8], state: &mut [u8; 40], inp: &[u8], inlen: usize)` - finalize with padding\n4. `sha256(out: &mut [u8], inp: &[u8], inlen: usize)` - one-shot\n5. `sha512_inc_init(state: &mut [u8; 72])` - init with IV, zero counter at bytes 64-71\n6. `sha512_inc_blocks(state: &mut [u8; 72], inp: &[u8], inblocks: usize)` - process full 128-byte blocks\n7. `sha512_inc_finalize(out: &mut [u8], state: &mut [u8; 72], inp: &[u8], inlen: usize)` - finalize\n8. `sha512(out: &mut [u8], inp: &[u8], inlen: usize)` - one-shot\n9. `mgf1_256(out: &mut [u8], outlen: usize, inp: &[u8], inlen: usize)` - MGF1 with SHA-256\n10. `mgf1_512(out: &mut [u8], outlen: usize, inp: &[u8], inlen: usize)` - MGF1 with SHA-512\n11. `seed_state(ctx: &mut crate::context::SpxCtx)` - absorb pub_seed into state_seeded (and state_seeded_512 if SPX_SHA512)\n\nKey implementation details:\n\nState format: SHA-256 state is 32 bytes (8x u32 big-endian) + 8 bytes (u64 big-endian byte counter). SHA-512 state is 64 bytes (8x u64 big-endian) + 8 bytes (u64 big-endian byte counter).\n\nHelper functions:\n- `load_bigendian_32(x: &[u8]) -> u32`\n- `load_bigendian_64(x: &[u8]) -> u64`\n- `store_bigendian_32(x: &mut [u8], u: u64)` - note: takes u64 but only uses lower 32 bits\n- `store_bigendian_64(x: &mut [u8], u: u64)`\n\nSHA-256 uses standard round constants (K256). The compression function `crypto_hashblocks_sha256` processes state as 8 big-endian u32 values with the standard SHA-256 schedule.\n\nSHA-256 IV: `[0x6a09e667, 0xbb67ae85, 0x3c6ef372, 0xa54ff53a, 0x510e527f, 0x9b05688c, 0x1f83d9ab, 0x5be0cd19]` stored as big-endian bytes.\n\nSHA-512 IV stored as big-endian bytes:\n```\n0x6a, 0x09, 0xe6, 0x67, 0xf3, 0xbc, 0xc9, 0x08, 0xbb, 0x67, 0xae,\n0x85, 0x84, 0xca, 0xa7, 0x3b, 0x3c, 0x6e, 0xf3, 0x72, 0xfe, 0x94,\n0xf8, 0x2b, 0xa5, 0x4f, 0xf5, 0x3a, 0x5f, 0x1d, 0x36, 0xf1, 0x51,\n0x0e, 0x52, 0x7f, 0xad, 0xe6, 0x82, 0xd1, 0x9b, 0x05, 0x68, 0x8c,\n0x2b, 0x3e, 0x6c, 0x1f, 0x1f, 0x83, 0xd9, 0xab, 0xfb, 0x41, 0xbd,\n0x6b, 0x5b, 0xe0, 0xcd, 0x19, 0x13, 0x7e, 0x21, 0x79\n```\n\nSHA-256 finalize padding:\n- Hash remaining bytes, keeping inlen & 63 as leftover\n- Pad: 0x80, zeros, 8-byte big-endian bit length\n- If leftover < 56: single 64-byte padded block\n- If leftover >= 56: two 64-byte padded blocks\n- Bit length = bytes * 8, stored as: `padded[56] = (bytes >> 53)` etc.\n\nSHA-512 finalize padding:\n- Hash remaining bytes, keeping inlen & 127 as leftover\n- If leftover < 112: single 128-byte padded block\n- If leftover >= 112: two 128-byte padded blocks (256 bytes)\n- Bit length stored starting at byte 119 (or 247 for double block): `padded[119] = (bytes >> 61)` etc.\n\nSHA-256 round constants (K256):\n```\n0x428a2f98, 0x71374491, 0xb5c0fbcf, 0xe9b5dba5,\n0x3956c25b, 0x59f111f1, 0x923f82a4, 0xab1c5ed5,\n0xd807aa98, 0x12835b01, 0x243185be, 0x550c7dc3,\n0x72be5d74, 0x80deb1fe, 0x9bdc06a7, 0xc19bf174,\n0xe49b69c1, 0xefbe4786, 0x0fc19dc6, 0x240ca1cc,\n0x2de92c6f, 0x4a7484aa, 0x5cb0a9dc, 0x76f988da,\n0x983e5152, 0xa831c66d, 0xb00327c8, 0xbf597fc7,\n0xc6e00bf3, 0xd5a79147, 0x06ca6351, 0x14292967,\n0x27b70a85, 0x2e1b2138, 0x4d2c6dfc, 0x53380d13,\n0x650a7354, 0x766a0abb, 0x81c2c92e, 0x92722c85,\n0xa2bfe8a1, 0xa81a664b, 0xc24b8b70, 0xc76c51a3,\n0xd192e819, 0xd6990624, 0xf40e3585, 0x106aa070,\n0x19a4c116, 0x1e376c08, 0x2748774c, 0x34b0bcb5,\n0x391c0cb3, 0x4ed8aa4a, 0x5b9cca4f, 0x682e6ff3,\n0x748f82ee, 0x78a5636f, 0x84c87814, 0x8cc70208,\n0x90befffa, 0xa4506ceb, 0xbef9a3f7, 0xc67178f2,\n```\n\nSHA-512 round constants (K512) - all 80 values as u64.\n\nThe compression function structure:\n- Load state as big-endian integers\n- For each 64-byte block: load 16 message words, do 64 rounds with message schedule expansion\n- Update state\n- Store state as big-endian integers\n\nFor `crypto_hashblocks_sha256`: returns remaining bytes (inlen after processing full blocks). Uses wrapping arithmetic throughout.\n\nFor `mgf1_256`: concatenate input with 4-byte big-endian counter, SHA-256 hash, output. Use `crate::utils::u32_to_bytes` for the counter.\n\nFor `seed_state`:\n```rust\npub fn seed_state(ctx: &mut crate::context::SpxCtx) {\n    let mut block = [0u8; 128]; // SPX_SHA512_BLOCK_BYTES\n    block[..crate::params::SPX_N].copy_from_slice(&ctx.pub_seed);\n    // rest is zeros\n    \n    sha256_inc_init(&mut ctx.state_seeded);\n    sha256_inc_blocks(&mut ctx.state_seeded, &block, 1);\n    \n    #[cfg(all(feature = \"sha2\", any(feature = \"192s\", feature = \"192f\", feature = \"256s\", feature = \"256f\")))]\n    {\n        sha512_inc_init(&mut ctx.state_seeded_512);\n        sha512_inc_blocks(&mut ctx.state_seeded_512, &block, 1);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nUse `.wrapping_add()`, `.wrapping_shr()`, `.rotate_right()` for all arithmetic.\n\nWrite ONLY the file, no explanations.","agentId":"ae5afc86d5b31e6aa","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The file has been written at `/tmp/harvest-translate-qHL6TU/translated_rust/src/sha2_impl.rs`. It implements:\n\n- Big-endian load/store helpers (`load_bigendian_32/64`, `store_bigendian_32/64`)\n- SHA-256 and SHA-512 round constants (K256, K512)\n- SHA-256/512 compression helper functions (Ch, Maj, Sigma0/1, sigma0/1 for both 32-bit and 64-bit variants)\n- `crypto_hashblocks_sha256` and `crypto_hashblocks_sha512` block compression functions\n- Incremental hashing API: `sha256_inc_init/blocks/finalize` and `sha512_inc_init/blocks/finalize`\n- One-shot `sha256` and `sha512`\n- `mgf1_256` and `mgf1_512` using `crate::utils::u32_to_bytes` for the counter\n- `seed_state` with conditional SHA-512 seeding via `#[cfg]`\n\nAll arithmetic uses wrapping operations (`.wrapping_add()`, `.rotate_right()`). The padding follows the C conventions with `bytes >> 53` style encoding for SHA-256 and `bytes >> 61` style for SHA-512."}],"totalDurationMs":209634,"totalTokens":38752,"totalToolUseCount":11,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":309,"cache_read_input_tokens":38124,"output_tokens":318,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":309},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
