{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JqmehwTfRWrL2RqFu5BMgt","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build succeeded with only warnings (no errors). All compilation errors have been fixed.\n\nHere is a summary of what was done:\n\n**Errors fixed:**\n\n1. **`src/sha2_impl.rs:489`** - Added `#[cfg(feature = \"sha2\")]` attribute to the `seed_state` function, since it references `ctx.state_seeded` which only exists when the `sha2` feature is enabled.\n\n2. **`src/sha2_impl.rs:142`** - Changed `let mut state: [u32; 8]` to `let _state: [u32; 8]` (unused variable, prefixed with underscore and removed `mut`).\n\n3. **`src/utils.rs:57,60`** - Fixed borrow checker errors by cloning `buffer` to a `tmp` variable before calling `thash::thash`, so the mutable and immutable borrows don't overlap.\n\n4. **`src/wots.rs:54`** - Fixed borrow checker error by copying `lengths[..SPX_WOTS_LEN1]` to a `msg_copy` Vec before passing it to `wots_checksum`.\n\n5. **`src/fips202.rs:416`** - Removed `mut` from `let mut remaining`.\n\n6. **`src/haraka_impl.rs`** - Removed `mut` from variable declarations in `br_aes_ct64_bitslice_Sbox` and `br_aes_ct_bitslice_Sbox` functions (the Sbox functions only assign once to these variables, never mutate them).\n\n7. **`src/haraka_impl.rs:894,939`** - Fixed double mutable borrow of array elements by using `split_at_mut(4)` to get non-overlapping mutable slices for `br_aes_ct64_interleave_in` calls.\n\n8. **`src/haraka_impl.rs:1048,1059,1063,1091,1113,1143,1164,1175`** - Fixed borrow checker errors with `haraka512_perm(&mut s, &s.clone(), ctx)` by cloning into a separate variable first before the function call.\n\n9. **`src/haraka_impl.rs:1135`** - Removed `mut` from `let mut idx` in `haraka_S_inc_squeeze`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a0175312786a91b3e (use SendMessage with to: 'a0175312786a91b3e' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 46285\ntool_uses: 40\nduration_ms: 149338</usage>"}]}